<!-- Token Efficiency: Real Numbers                                      -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->

<div class="section-alt" style="background:#1f1a11;padding:3rem 2rem;margin:2rem 0;">
  <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;">
    <h2 style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Token Efficiency: Measured, With Its Lane</h2>
    <p style="text-align:center;color:#9a9082;margin-bottom:2rem;font-size:0.9rem;">Every figure below names the metric type, the tokenizer, the baseline and N, per TEMSpec &sect;6.3. Nothing here is a bare percentage, and nothing here compares one tokenizer against another across two languages.</p>

    <div style="display:flex;gap:2rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      <div style="text-align:center;padding:1.5rem 2rem;background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;">
        <div style="font-size:2.5rem;font-weight:700;color:#6fc2b2;">24.6%</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#9a9082;margin-top:0.3rem;">FEWER TOKENS, toke v0.4 vs toke v0.3</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#6b6356;">cl100k_base on both sides &middot; 4,787 vs 6,347 &middot; N = 60 Gate-1 tasks</div>
      </div>
      <div style="text-align:center;padding:1.5rem 2rem;background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;">
        <div style="font-size:2.5rem;font-weight:700;color:#f0c04a;">1.34&times;</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#9a9082;margin-top:0.3rem;">toke COSTS MORE THAN PYTHON</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#6b6356;">[1.22, 1.48] &middot; cl100k_base on both sides &middot; 4,787 vs 3,565 &middot; N = 60</div>
      </div>
      <div style="text-align:center;padding:1.5rem 2rem;background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;">
        <div style="font-size:2.5rem;font-weight:700;color:#f0c040;">0.92&times;</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#9a9082;margin-top:0.3rem;">BYTES, toke vs PYTHON</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#6b6356;">raw UTF-8, no tokenizer &middot; 693 vs 753 &middot; N = 4 verified pairs</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="text-align:center;color:#9a9082;font-size:0.85rem;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;"><strong style="color:#f5efe2">What was withdrawn, and why.</strong> The &ldquo;52% average token reduction vs cl100k&rdquo; that used to headline this section compared <em>two tokenizers over one toke text</em> (Toke-16K v0.3 vs cl100k_base, N&nbsp;=&nbsp;42) &mdash; never a comparison with Python &mdash; and it cannot be reproduced from the dataset it cited. It is withdrawn, not requalified. On canonical v0.4 <code style="background:#2a2317;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:3px;padding:0.15em 0.35em;font-size:0.82em;color:#f0c04a;">tkc --min</code> text the shipped 8K tokenizer needs <strong>15.4% more</strong> tokens than cl100k_base (279,672 vs 242,427; N&nbsp;=&nbsp;2,000). No &ldquo;purpose-built tokenizer beats cl100k&rdquo; claim is supportable until a correct v0.4 tokenizer is trained and locked. Source: <code style="background:#2a2317;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:3px;padding:0.15em 0.35em;font-size:0.82em;color:#f0c04a;">docs/metrics-baseline.md</code>. See the <a href="/roadmap" style="color:#f0c04a;">roadmap</a> for what is measured next.</p>

    <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:1.5rem;display:flex;gap:1rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <a href="/tokenizer" style="background:#2a2317;border:1px solid #f0c04a;color:#f0c04a;padding:0.6rem 1.2rem;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:600;">Try the Live Tokenizer &rarr;</a>
      <a href="/tokens" style="background:#2a2317;border:1px solid #6b6356;color:#9a9082;padding:0.6rem 1.2rem;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;">Token Visualisation Gallery</a>
      <a href="/docs/reference/token-comparison" style="background:#2a2317;border:1px solid #6b6356;color:#9a9082;padding:0.6rem 1.2rem;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;">Token comparison reference</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

