<div class="section-heading">
  <h2>Available Across Multiple Platforms</h2>
</div>
<p class="section-desc">toke tooling is published on npm, PyPI, Ollama, HuggingFace, VS Code, and more. Pick the one that fits your workflow.</p>

<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:1rem;max-width:1100px;margin:1.5rem auto 3rem;">
  <div style="background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;padding:1.2rem;">
    <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:0 0 0.5rem;color:#f0c04a;">Ollama</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#9a9082;margin:0 0 0.8rem;">Run locally. No cloud, no API key. 4.4GB download.</p>
    <code style="display:block;background:#14110b;padding:0.5rem 0.75rem;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.8rem;color:#6fc2b2;">ollama run karwalski/toke</code>
  </div>
  <div style="background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;padding:1.2rem;">
    <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:0 0 0.5rem;color:#f0c04a;">VS Code</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#9a9082;margin:0 0 0.8rem;">Syntax highlighting, snippets, companion files, LSP diagnostics.</p>
    <code style="display:block;background:#14110b;padding:0.5rem 0.75rem;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.8rem;color:#6fc2b2;">ext install tokelang.toke-language</code>
  </div>
  <div style="background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;padding:1.2rem;">
    <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:0 0 0.5rem;color:#f0c04a;">MCP Server</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#9a9082;margin:0 0 0.8rem;">15 tools for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and any MCP client.</p>
    <code style="display:block;background:#14110b;padding:0.5rem 0.75rem;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.8rem;color:#6fc2b2;">npx @tokelang/mcp-server</code>
  </div>
  <div style="background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;padding:1.2rem;">
    <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:0 0 0.5rem;color:#f0c04a;">REST API</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#9a9082;margin:0 0 0.8rem;">Generate toke code from any language. Free tier available.</p>
    <code style="display:block;background:#14110b;padding:0.5rem 0.75rem;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.8rem;color:#6fc2b2;">curl api.tokelang.dev/v1/generate</code>
  </div>
  <div style="background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;padding:1.2rem;">
    <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:0 0 0.5rem;color:#f0c04a;">Python Tokenizer</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#9a9082;margin:0 0 0.8rem;">Count tokens, measure compression. Pure Python, no deps.</p>
    <code style="display:block;background:#14110b;padding:0.5rem 0.75rem;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.8rem;color:#6fc2b2;">pip install toke-tokenizer</code>
  </div>
  <div style="background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;padding:1.2rem;">
    <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:0 0 0.5rem;color:#f0c04a;">HuggingFace</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#9a9082;margin:0 0 0.8rem;">AWQ 4-bit model + BPE tokenizer. Fine-tune or self-host.</p>
    <a href="https://huggingface.co/karwalski/toke" style="color:#6fc2b2;font-size:0.8rem;text-decoration:none;">huggingface.co/karwalski/toke &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div style="background:#1f1a11;border:1px solid #2a2317;border-radius:8px;padding:1.2rem;">
    <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:0 0 0.5rem;color:#f0c04a;">Docker</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#9a9082;margin:0 0 0.8rem;">Self-host the full inference stack. GPU or CPU mode.</p>
    <code style="display:block;background:#14110b;padding:0.5rem 0.75rem;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.8rem;color:#6fc2b2;">docker compose up</code>
